        "math_academy_id": "q-10559",
        "problem": "Calculate\n$\\int (4{cos}^{2}\u2061x-2)\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        "worked_solution": "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}\u2061x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x=2{cos}^{2}\u2061x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}\u2061x=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{cos}^{2}\u2061x-2)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (4(\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x+1))-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (2\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x+2-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int 2\\operatorname{cos}\u20612x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x)+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
